  "unreadable": [],
  "notes": "Each I/O pad has a large and a small hole for the same signal (2 sized holes); recorded as one position per pad. Labels use the Arduino D/A names with silkscreen numbers first in functions. D2/D14 added to SDA/SCL from the separate I2C callout block. 2-pin battery JST (only +/- marks) and the button skipped.",
  "uncertain": [
    "RST: a small hole labeled RST sits between pads 16 and 0 on the right side; its callout (RST/Reset) is placed apart from the pad rows, so placing it in the right-pads row is inferred from silkscreen",
    "Top I2C: two printed label lines (GND 3.3V SDA SCL / SDA 3.3V GND SCL) above the 0.1in header holes and the 4-pin JST; which line belongs to the header and which to the JST is not explicit (assumed upper line = header holes, lower line = JST)"
  ]
